# HRMS brand guidelines

Read and follow [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md) before adding or changing any UI. Do not invent a second visual language.

## Must match

- Zinc / near-black primary (`bg-zinc-900` / `text-zinc-950`). Status color only on badges and deltas (emerald / amber / red).
- App pages live in `w-full min-h-full border border-border rounded-2xl p-6 bg-surface flex flex-col gap-6`.
- Page H1: `text-h1 font-medium`. Subtitle: `text-body-lg text-zinc-500 font-medium`.
- Primary button: `rounded-lg bg-zinc-900 hover:bg-zinc-800 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-2xs active:scale-98`.
- Secondary: bordered `bg-surface hover:bg-surface-hover`.
- Charts: grayscale zinc gradients only (`#E4E4E7` → `#18181B`). No rainbow series.
- Font: Geist Sans. Icons: existing `components/icons` + Lucide. No new typeface or icon pack.
- Dark mode: keep `zinc-*` classes that `app/globals.css` already remaps; prefer `surface` / `text-primary` / `border` tokens for new chrome.

## Do not

- Blue primary CTAs (`#1D4ED8` / `primary-hover`)
- Heavy shadows on tables or KPI cards
- Centered in-app page titles
- Replacing sidebar custom icons with Lucide
- New marketing motion on `/admin` or `/employee` routes
